==English==

===Etymology===
Compound of {{compound|red|neck|lang=en}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|slang|pejorative|lang=en}} An uneducated, unsophisticated, or poor [[white]] person, typically used to describe residents (of any gender<ref>)[http://www.hit-country-music-lyrics.com/redneck-woman-lyrics.html Country Music Lyrics New Country Tunes]</ref> of the [[rural]] [[Southern United States]].
# {{context|slang|lang=en}} The nickname given to miners who wore red [[bandana]]s for identification during the West Virginia mine war of 1921.<ref>[http://www.wvculture.org/hiStory/minewars.html West Virginia Division of Culture and History]</ref>
# {{context|UK|archaic|lang=en}} The nickname given to [[Roman Catholics]] in the nineteenth and twentieth centuries.

====Synonyms====
* [[cracker]], [[hick]], [[hillbilly]], [[peckerwood]], [[white trash]]

====Derived terms====
* [[redneckish]]
* [[redneckism]]
* [[rednecky]]

